  "text": "proprium.sacratissimi-cordis-iesu-evangelium",
  "about": "The Gospel of the feast of the Most Sacred Heart of Jesus, John 19:31–37. A soldier opens the side of the dead Christ with a lance, and blood and water immediately flow forth.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time the Jews, because it was the Parasceve, that the bodies might not remain upon the cross on the Sabbath—for that Sabbath was a great day—besought Pilate that their legs might be broken and that they might be taken away." },
    "s02": { "translation": "The soldiers therefore came, and they broke the legs of the first and of the other who was crucified with Him." },
    "s03": { "translation": "But after they were come to Jesus, when they saw that He was already dead, they did not break His legs; but one of the soldiers opened His side with a lance, and immediately there came out blood and water." },
    "s04": { "translation": "And he that saw it hath given testimony, and his testimony is true. And he knoweth that he saith true, that you also may believe." },
    "s05": { "translation": "For these things were done that the Scripture might be fulfilled: You shall not break a bone of Him. And again another Scripture saith: They shall look on Him whom they pierced." }
  },
